From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stage C <stage-c@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 20 Nov 2026 16:10:00 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] hoist loop-invariant aggregate field reads

sroa promotes a local only when its address is never taken, so a `Vec`
local that was written before a loop stays in its stack slot and every
field read inside the loop goes to memory. This pass reads such a field
once in the preheader into a fresh local and replaces the in-loop read
with a copy of that local. The original destination assignment stays in
the loop, so a zero-trip loop leaves it untouched.

It relies on MIR being borrow-checked: a direct read of `base.field`
cannot coexist with a live unique borrow of `base`, and a shared borrow
cannot write a `Freeze` base. Raw pointers are outside those guarantees,
so a raw pointer to a local (not through a dereference), a cast to a raw
pointer from a reference, or an integer-to-pointer cast skips the
function. That is not yet enough for unsafe code: a call can still hand
back a raw pointer into the base.

The preheader read is paid once per loop entry, so the pass only
optimizes loops that are part of a nest (nested in another loop, or
containing one). A single-level loop over a runtime-length collection
can execute too few times to pay for it: the first suite run regressed
`expr` by 0.01% entirely because of `expr::Env::set`'s short lookup
loop. With the nest gate, a local A/B gives `expr` 0.000%, `nbody`
-10.551% and `b_alloc` -1.731%.

The pass is opt-in through the unstable flag
`-Zmir-hoist-loop-field-reads`, off by default. It must not run in the
compiler, sysroot or default benchmark builds: at level 2 the stage-1
compiler runs it over rustc's own crates while building rustc.wasm, and
an earlier always-on version miscompiled the compiler (a dataflow bounds
panic while building the pure sysroot in CI). The benchmark and difftest
scripts opt the clif compile in through BENCH_MIR_HOIST=1 and
DIFFTEST_MIR_HOIST=1, and the cranelift_wasm workflow exposes the same
switch as the `mir_hoist` workflow_dispatch input. Experiment points are
not published to the benchmark chart.

This is the first SROA increment from Goal 1 step 5b. The cost-model
inliner and the suite measurement are still to come; the pass makes no
speed claim. It is a local experiment for the CogWasm pipeline, not an
upstream contribution; its code and comments are LLM-generated under the
personal-use exemption and a human must review and own it.

---
